blem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD to understand what R1.1-R1.4 require for mv\n   - Read cp/main.go and cp/cp_test.go to understand the established patterns for file operation utilities\n   - Key design insight: mv differs from cp in that (1) it uses `os.Rename` for same-filesystem moves, (2) it doesn't require `-r` for directories, (3) for cross-filesystem moves it must copy then delete source, (4) verbose format differs\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Massive task prompt with full project context, SRDs, architecture, execution constitution, go style constitution, package contracts, shared protocols, and the specific task description for implementing cmd/mv R1.1-R1.4. Includes explicit constraints about not running git commands, not modifying files outside scope, writing all files before building, etc.\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" — Instructs to create a detailed summary of the conversation so far.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/mv/main.go` implementing srd057-mv R1.1-R1.4 (basic move and rename)\n   - Create `cmd/mv/mv_test.go` with differential tests covering each of R1.1-R1.4\n   - Run `go build -o bin/mv ./cmd/mv/` to verify compilation\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/mv/...` to check for issues\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/mv/... -count=1` to verify tests pass/skip\n   - Verify all 5 acceptance criteria (AC1-AC5)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just completed the research phase — reading the SRD (srd057-mv.yaml), the reference implementation (cmd/cp/main.go), and the reference test file (cmd/cp/cp_test.go). I was about to plan and implement the two files. The implementation needs to:\n   \n   For `cmd/mv/main.go`:\n   - Call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main\n   - Parse flags manually (following cp pattern) — for R1.x scope, minimal flag parsing needed but should include `--` support\n   - Implement `moveSingle(src, dest)`: if dest is dir, move into it (R1.4); use `os.Rename` first, fall